---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Calileus | Software Architect" description="Software Architect and Lead Developer focused on dependable high-stakes software systems." lang="en">
  <section class="section-band section-intro border-t-0">
    <p class="eyebrow">Software Architect</p>
    <h1>I build dependable software systems for high-stakes products.</h1>
    <p>Software Architect with 10+ years in modern C++, quality engineering, and delivery leadership. I turn complex requirements into production-ready architecture and repeatable execution.</p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <a href="/experience" class="btn-primary">View experience</a>
      <a href="/projects" class="btn-secondary">Explore projects</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-band">
    <div class="grid-3">
      <article class="impact-item"><strong>58+</strong><span>Releases delivered, including customer-facing production programs.</span></article>
      <article class="impact-item"><strong>60%</strong><span>Review effort reduction through automated quality gates and CI workflows.</span></article>
      <article class="impact-item"><strong>14</strong><span>Engineers led across architecture, implementation, validation, and deployment.</span></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-band">
    <div class="grid-2">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Focus</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Architecture & Quality</h2>
        <p>Component boundaries, event-driven design, MISRA discipline, static analysis, and CI/CD gates that improve reliability and delivery speed.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Current role</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">AUMOVIO / Continental</h2>
        <p>Software Architect & Lead Developer for Automotive Radar Logic Model, owning the path from quotation and architecture definition to production deployment.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>